    "conclusion": "Given the significantly higher chance of saving a life, Ellis should provisionally give the blanket to Rowan, although this breaks the earlier promise to Sasha.",
    "strongest_objection": "Breaking the promise to Sasha violates a clear duty of fidelity that normally binds even when circumstances change.",
    "answer_to_objection": "The rescue duty is weightier here because the difference between an 80% and a 60% survival chance is morally significant enough to override the prima facie promise; fulfilling the promise would foreseeably allow a preventable death with higher probability.",
    "reversal_condition": "If the survival chances were equal or Sasha’s chance were higher, the promise-keeping duty would no longer be overridden, shifting the decision to honoring the promise.",
    "residual_disagreement": [
      "Some maintain that promises are categorical and cannot be overridden by probabilistic benefits, so they would still choose B."
    ]
